WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.870
England: 6.3 million properties sit in
areas at risk of flooding from rivers,

2
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.450
the sea or surface water.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.570
Cities can even add rain.

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.570
Around six US cities, satellite radar
found monthly rainfall rates about 28 per

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.810
cent higher downwind.

6
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.390
Then the rain lands on
roofs, roads and paving.

7
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.070
So where does all that water go, and
why does it reach the river so fast?

8
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.730
In this mission, you'll trace rain
through the urban water cycle,

9
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.910
and read the hydrograph it leaves behind.

10
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.250
Then you'll design drainage
that copies nature,

11
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.890
and judge whether it is
enough for a big city.

12
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.770
Your mission: explain
where city rain goes,

13
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.510
and why it reaches the river so fast.
